NAME
    mkdir - make a directory

SYNOPSIS
    mkdir path

DESCRIPTION
    Makes a new, empty directory: 4 sectors, room for 62 entries
    besides "." and "..". Quiet on success; "cannot mkdir" when the
    name exists, the parent is missing or full, or the name is not
    valid. mkdir is a shell built-in; the MKDIR syscall (8), which
    cp -r uses, does the same work.

    It stays in the shell because it is a bootstrap primitive: a fresh
    card needs it to make /BIN before any /BIN program exists.

LIMITS
    Names are 1..12 characters; the path at most 62. Refused ("cannot
    mkdir") while a file is open for writing, which includes a > or
    >> redirect and a pipe: a directory is allocated at the same free
    pointer (see shell).

EXAMPLES
    mkdir /T
    mkdir SUB           in the current directory

NOTES
    Changed from the P8X version: nothing is printed on success (the
    P8X said "DIR CREATED").
    The command is the Y1/OS shell's own (os/y1os.c); the page is
    ported from P8X os/man/mkdir 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    rmdir, cd, dir, cp, shell
